  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f_d(n)$ be the minimal $m$ such that any set of $m$ points in $\\mathbb{R}^d$ contains a set of $n$ points such that any two determined distances are distinct. Estimate $f_d(n)$. In particular, is it true that, for fixed $n\\geq 3$, $ f_d(n)=2^{o(d)}? $ ",
